<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/" x:xmptk="Adobe XMP Core 5.6-c017 91.164464, 2020/06/15-10:20:05        ">
   <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
      <rdf:Description rdf:about=""
            xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"
            xmlns:xmp="http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/"
            xmlns:pdf="http://ns.adobe.com/pdf/1.3/"
            xmlns:xmpMM="http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/mm/"
            xmlns:illustrator="http://ns.adobe.com/illustrator/1.0/">
         <dc:format>application/pdf</dc:format>
         <dc:title>
            <rdf:Alt>
               <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">NCP1216, NCP1216A - PWM Current-Mode Controller for High-Power Universal Off-Line Supplies</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Alt>
         </dc:title>
         <dc:creator>
            <rdf:Seq>
               <rdf:li>ON Semiconductor</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Seq>
         </dc:creator>
         <dc:description>
            <rdf:Alt>
               <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Housed in a SOICâˆ’8 or PDIPâˆ’7 package, the NCP1216 represents&#xD;&#xA;an enhanced version of NCP1200 based controllers. Due to its high&#xD;&#xA;drive capability, NCP1216 drives large gateâˆ’charge MOSFETs, which&#xD;&#xA;together with internal ramp compensation and builtâˆ’in frequency&#xD;&#xA;jittering, ease the design of modern ACâˆ’DC adapters.&#xD;&#xA;With an internal structure operating at different fixed frequencies,&#xD;&#xA;the controller supplies itself from the highâˆ’voltage rail, avoiding the&#xD;&#xA;need of an auxiliary winding. This feature naturally eases the designer&#xD;&#xA;task in some particular applications, e.g. battery chargers or TV sets.&#xD;&#xA;Currentâˆ’mode control also provides an excellent input audio&#xD;&#xA;susceptibility and inherent pulseâˆ’byâˆ’pulse control. Internal ramp&#xD;&#xA;compensation easily prevents subâˆ’harmonic oscillations from taking&#xD;&#xA;place in continuous conduction mode designs.&#xD;&#xA;When the current setpoint falls below a given value, e.g. the output&#xD;&#xA;power demand diminishes, the IC automatically enters the soâˆ’called&#xD;&#xA;skip cycle mode and provides excellent efficiency at light loads.&#xD;&#xA;Because this occurs at a user adjustable low peak current, no acoustic&#xD;&#xA;noise takes place.&#xD;&#xA;The NCP1216 features an efficient protective circuitry, which in&#xD;&#xA;presence of an over current condition disables the output pulses while&#xD;&#xA;the device enters a safe burst mode, trying to restart. Once the default&#xD;&#xA;has gone, the device autoâˆ’recovers.</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Alt>
         </dc:description>
         <xmp:CreateDate>2016-05-26T16:40:46-07:00</xmp:CreateDate>
         <xmp:CreatorTool>BroadVision, Inc.</xmp:CreatorTool>
         <xmp:ModifyDate>2020-08-31T08:29:53+02:00</xmp:ModifyDate>
         <xmp:MetadataDate>2020-08-31T08:29:53+02:00</xmp:MetadataDate>
